Usage: millstream replay --pipeline=PIPELINE [<id> ...] [flags]

Replay dead letters into their run, or a step over past items.

Three forms, exclusive: --from dlq, --step or --stream.

Examples:
  # Retry a run's open dead letters in that run
  millstream replay --pipeline listings --from dlq --run <run>
  # Rerun a step over the items published in the last day, in a new replay run
  millstream replay --pipeline listings --step score --since 1d
  # Back-fill an imported stream from the producer's retained items
  millstream replay --pipeline scoring --stream listings.ready

Arguments:
  [<id> ...]   With --from dlq, the dead letters to replay; all of the run's open ones when none.

Flags:
  --from=SOURCE               Replay dead letters into their run: --from dlq, the one source.
                              Exclusive with --step and --stream; one of the three is required.
  --step=STEP                 Start a replay run of this step over past items on its input streams.
  --stream=STREAM             Start a replay run back-filling this imported stream from the
                              producer's retained items on it.
  --pipeline=PIPELINE         Pipeline name.
  --run=RUN                   With --from dlq, the run whose dead letters to replay; with --step,
                              replay only this run's items.
  --migrate                   With --from dlq, move the run to the pipeline's active revision first.
  --since=SINCE               With --step or --stream, replay only the items published within this
                              duration (7d, 12h).
  --where=WHERE               With --step or --stream, replay only the items for which this CEL
                              expression holds.
  --revision=N                With --step or --stream, the revision to run on (default: the active
                              one).
  --request-id=REQUEST_ID     With --step or --stream, the request id naming the replay run;
                              repeating it starts nothing new.
  --var=KEY=VALUE;...         With --step or --stream, set a variable (name=value).

Global flags:
  --db=DSN                    Store DSN, overriding store.dsn: sqlite://<path> (created with its
                              directory) or postgres://host/db (default:
                              sqlite://.millstream/millstream.db).
  --env-file=ENV_FILE         Environment file (default: $MILLSTREAM_ENV_FILE, else
                              ./millstream.yaml when it exists).
  --server=URL                Change state through the API of the engine serving at this URL
                              (default: $MILLSTREAM_SERVER; token: $MILLSTREAM_TOKEN).
  --direct                    Change state from this process, not through --server; on Postgres this
                              takes the leadership lock, waiting while an engine runs.
  --color=auto|always|never   Color the help: auto (on a terminal, unless NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb),
                              always or never (default: $MILLSTREAM_COLOR, else auto).
